From 97c09a7abe3f338a382fba358ebf87c775cd0e86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TBD <tbd@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:32:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(heading-hierarchy): demote section headers that a
 complete PDF outline does not list

Add the opt-in option HeadingHierarchyOptions.demote_unmatched_headings (default False).
When the PDF bookmarks look complete, a detected section header that matches no bookmark
becomes a text item. Standard unnumbered headings (Abstract, Keywords, Acknowledgements,
References, Bibliography, Appendix) are kept, matched headings keep the bookmark level, and
body text is never promoted.

The outline counts as complete only when all of these are true:
- it has more than one level;
- every detected dotted-numbered heading ("2.1 ...") matches a bookmark;
- at least half of the detected headings match a bookmark;
- no two headings to demote share a heading-like style (larger than the body text, bold,
  or set in a font face other than the body face).

The style check reads the parsed pages, so the stage now also keeps them when only this
option needs them. Without parsed pages, nothing is demoted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
